---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="What to Expect | Bransky Fitness, Pleasanton"
  description="What training with Mark Bransky looks like: a movement assessment first, then a customized strength and conditioning program built around functional movement and weight management."
  path="/training/"
  activeNav="training"
>

  <section class="page-intro facets">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>What to expect</h1>
      <p>Experience a transformative fitness journey with tailored personal training solutions. Unlock your potential with expert guidance and dedicated support. Start your path to success today.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-dark facets-dark" aria-label="The training process">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="process-row">
        <figure class="process-photo">
          <img src="/images/hero-squat.jpg" alt="Mark Bransky observing a client's squat form on turf flooring in the studio" width="2000" height="1400" loading="eager">
        </figure>
        <div class="process-copy">
          <p class="process-eyebrow">Assess your starting point</p>
          <h3>We begin with a sit-down discussion</h3>
          <p>I ask you a lot of questions about your goals, training history, injury and health history, and lifestyle. Then we assess your movement quality to identify imbalances and inspire a safe and effective program.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="process-row reverse">
        <figure class="process-photo">
          <img src="/images/training-lunge.jpg" alt="Mark Bransky coaching a client through a kettlebell lunge in the studio" width="2000" height="1400" loading="lazy">
        </figure>
        <div class="process-copy">
          <p class="process-eyebrow">Your program</p>
          <h3>Customized, and built to make you independent</h3>
          <p>I build a customized program and work with you to develop your comfort and confidence with it. Though some clients prefer to strictly train with me, I'm going to try to make you as functionally independent as possible. I never ask for long commitments. I need to keep earning your business every step of the way while creating a valuable experience and relationship you want to return to.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="programs-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="programs-heading">Programs</h2>
        <p class="lede">Four ways clients work with Mark, from one-on-one correction to mentoring the next generation of trainers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="program-grid">
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Functional movement</h3>
          <p>For clients dealing with pain, past injury, or movement that just feels off. Sessions rebuild the fundamental patterns: squat, hinge, push, pull, and carry, so your body handles daily life and training without compensating around a weak link.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Strength &amp; conditioning</h3>
          <p>For clients ready to build capacity, not just correct it. Programming is structured and progressive, adjusted session to session as you get stronger.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Weight management</h3>
          <p>Training and habit coaching aimed at change you can actually keep, built around your schedule and history rather than a generic calorie target.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Trainer mentorship &amp; workshops</h3>
          <p>One-on-one mentoring and workshops for personal trainers who want to sharpen their assessment and coaching skills, drawing on Mark's work certifying over 1,000 trainers through NASM.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="cta-heading">Not sure which program fits?</h2>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Let's Go!</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
